<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47423" body-key="">*<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤνῑς</span></b> , ἡ, epith. of cows, of uncertain meaning (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>yearling</i>, fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνος</span> (c), acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				432.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>), used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in acc. sg. and pl.: gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤνῐος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.174
				</span></i>
			:—
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς . . ἤνῑς ἠκέστας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.94
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				275
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				309
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦν ἤνιν εὐρυμέτωπον ἀδμήτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.292
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.382
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦνιν</span> codd. and <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
			</span></i> Oroandae ap. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.71
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤνιν</span> Tyrannioibid.: perh.
			a stem in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span>.)</div>
